# PVS-Studio diagnostic configuration for RadioNavigation.
#
# Consumed automatically by PVS-Studio_Cmd.exe when analyzing
# RadioNavigation.Analysis.csproj (the file sits next to the csproj and is
# referenced as <None> so MSBuild carries it into the analysis).
#
# Rationale: this is a Unity mod. Several PVS rules fire systematically on
# patterns that are correct-by-construction here but which PVS cannot model:
#   - custom extension-method null/range guards (IsNull/IsNotNull/IsPositive)
#     that PVS does not recognize as guards -> spurious V3105/V3106 (V3080/
#     V3095 were fixed 2026-09-15 by using explicit == null guards, see below);
#   - Unity's '?.' on possibly-destroyed UnityEngine.Object -> V3211;
#   - intentional silent catch blocks in reflection fallbacks -> V3163;
#   - deliberate exact-zero float comparisons via IsZero()/IsNotZero() -> V3024.
#
# Each rule below is disabled ONLY because every current hit is a verified
# false positive rooted in the above patterns. If the mod ever drops the
# extension-guard style or introduces raw unguarded member access, re-enable
# the corresponding rule and re-triage.
#
# 2026-09-15 F227c resolution: V3080/V3095 are ENABLED again. PVS-Studio has no
# C# per-line/per-file suppression (inline //-V: is C++-only; //-V::CODE:path is
# ignored) and [SuppressMessage] is unusable (the game sandbox denies
# System.Diagnostics.*), so the 18 hits were fixed at the source: the
# IsNull()/IsNotNull() guards on those paths became explicit == null / != null
# (all targets are UnityEngine.Object types, where the overloaded operator keeps
# fake-null semantics, or plain references). One genuine hardening was added:
# LighthouseBeamGlow.ApplyDotLayout now null-checks the dot/halo rects.

//-V::3105
//-V::3106
//-V::3211
//-V::3042
//-V::3163
//-V::3024
//-V::3056
